  "answer": "Based on the National Archives data, here are the signers who meet all your criteria (born in the American colonies, not future presidents, died before the 1783 Treaty of Paris):\n\n**7 signers:**\n\n| Name | State | Birthplace | Date of Death |\n|------|-------|------------|---------------|\n| John Hart | NJ | Hunterdon Co., NJ | May 11, 1779 |\n| Joseph Hewes | NC | Kingston, NJ | October 10, 1779 |\n| Philip Livingston | NY | Albany, NY | June 12, 1778 |\n| Thomas Lynch Jr. | SC | Prince George's Parish, SC | c. 1779 |\n| John Morton | PA | Ridley Township, PA | c. 1777 |\n| George Ross | PA | New Castle, DE | July 14, 1779 |\n| Richard Stockton | NJ | Princeton, NJ | February 28, 1781 |\n\n**Excluded from the 56:**\n- **8 born outside the colonies**: Button Gwinnett (England), Francis Lewis (Wales), Robert Morris (England), James Smith (Ireland), George Taylor (Ireland), Matthew Thornton (Ireland), James Wilson (Scotland), John Witherspoon (Scotland)\n- **2 future presidents**: John Adams, Thomas Jefferson\n- **Remaining 39** either survived past 1783 or died after the Treaty of Paris (e.g., Caesar Rodney died June 1784, just after)",
